{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact clean head f904524fb2520f037f9dcc50b33fed685bd3499a, artifact 022cc91282f79f5a71d40d38529a904ecd7ea6fa.\n\nThe remedy is the fourth candidate the request offered: the result says how the fold read the act. `projected` carries the fold's ruling when it is anything other than plain effect, with its reason; any citation naming no event in this workroom; and, for a report, whether it became a review and which artifact it judges. The hook was already there — withKindWarning existed for the undefined-kind case, which is the same idea applied to one field.\n\nI chose it over the three key-policing candidates because those each fix one shape. Warning on a verdict-like key catches `status` on a report and says nothing about an approval that omits the artifact from rests_on, which is the version that has blocked merges three times, including one blocking right now. Four distinct versions of this trap have cost time today. Describing the reading covers the family, including versions nobody has hit.\n\nThe two trade-offs are stated in docs/reference/mcp/state.md rather than left implicit. Unknown body keys are still accepted: refusing them would catch `status` and permanently narrow a structure that is open so a room can carry vocabulary this implementation never anticipated, which is too much to give up for one spelling mistake. And the notes are a report, not a guarantee — they say what the fold made of the act at that moment, a later supersession can change any of it, and reading a summary is weaker than querying. The page says to treat clean notes as the absence of known traps rather than the presence of correctness.\n\nThe regression asserts each case separately rather than through a table, and every case is one that has actually happened here: a report that sets no verdict, a review whose artifact did not resolve, a citation naming nothing, an ineffective ruling. It also pins the quiet cases — an ordinary effective act is not annotated, a resolving citation is not reported as unresolved, and an unidentified act gets no invented notes.\n\nOn the gates, and this needs saying plainly rather than being rounded up. `go vet ./...` is clean and `go test ./...` passes except for TestWarmDepth20000SummaryLatencyAndSize in internal/statusview, which failed at p99 745ms against a 500ms bound during the full-suite run and passes in 6.5s when run alone. My change touches only cmd/gitseq-mcp and one reference page, so it does not reach that package, but I am reporting the failure rather than describing the suite as green. It is a third instance of the load-sensitive-bound family; I have recorded it as evidence on f6383a92 rather than filing another request.\n\nOne thing I got wrong and corrected: I began this edit in the main checkout rather than a worktree. I saved the diff, restored main, created request/mcp-projection-notes, and applied it there. Main is clean and carries none of it, but that is worth verifying rather than taking from me.","body":{"head":"f904524fb2520f037f9dcc50b33fed685bd3499a","status":"ready-for-review"}}